ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":59,"prev":61,"next":64,"titles":66,"firmware":235},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":13,"order":14,"path":15,"context":16,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":26,"procedures":49,"parameters":50,"related":51,"body":54,"sources":55,"official_url":30,"controls":58},"hardware.safety-and-care","Safety, care and warranty",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"warnings","safety","cleaning","temperature","warranty","phantom power","hearing","battery safety","hardware",80,"knowledge/manual/units/hardware/safety-and-care.md",{"modes":17,"screens":18},[],[],"TE's safety notes for connecting, charging, temperature, cleaning and the battery, and what the 12-month warranty covers.","current",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[27,32,35,38,40,42,45,47],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"connect","Switch every device off before cabling them together; when you have to plug in while running, plug the lead into the OP-XY before the other device.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy","official",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"phantom","Never run a cable from the OP-XY's jacks into a microphone input with phantom power switched on; it can damage the unit.",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"charging","Charge only from 5 V USB power, such as a computer's USB port or a USB charger.",{"id":8,"text":39,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"Use the unit between 10 and 35 °C (50–95 °F) and store it between 0 and 35 °C (32–86 °F).",{"id":7,"text":41,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"Wipe the shell with a slightly damp cloth and let it dry before use.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"battery","Do not charge or use a unit whose battery looks damaged; replacement batteries must come from TE and be fitted by qualified staff, and heat, fire or crushing can make a battery explode or leak.",{"id":11,"text":46,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"Avoid long listening sessions at high volume to protect your hearing.",{"id":9,"text":48,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"The unit is factory tested and has a 12-month warranty from the purchase date; it does not cover misuse (drops, crushing, wrong voltages on the connectors, faulty modifications) or shipping costs.",[],[],[52,53],"hardware.power-and-charging","hardware.in-the-box","The two that catch people out: phantom power on a mixer or interface channel the OP-XY is plugged\ninto, and charging from anything but plain 5 V USB.",[56],{"url":30,"kind":57},"guide",[],{"id":13,"title":60},"Hardware",{"id":62,"title":63},"hardware.system-menu","Function test and pot calibration (system menu)",{"id":53,"title":65},"Box contents and the factory-sound licence",{"basics.key-notation":67,"basics.main-modes":68,"basics.modules":69,"basics.track-buttons":70,"basics.linked-tracks":71,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":72,"basics.workflow":73,"basics.firmware-versions":74,"hardware.layout":75,"hardware.power-and-charging":76,"hardware.connectors":77,"hardware.specifications":78,"hardware.te-boot":79,"hardware.firmware-update":80,"hardware.factory-reset":81,"hardware.system-menu":63,"hardware.safety-and-care":3,"hardware.in-the-box":65,"sequencer.overview":82,"sequencer.step-entry":83,"sequencer.step-recording":84,"sequencer.live-recording":85,"sequencer.extend-notes":86,"sequencer.nudge":87,"sequencer.single-sound":88,"sequencer.rotate":89,"sequencer.copy-step":90,"sequencer.transpose-sequence":91,"sequencer.parameter-locks":92,"sequencer.clear-and-undo":93,"sequencer.step-components":94,"sequencer.step-component-reference":95,"sequencer.component-pulse":96,"sequencer.component-pulse-hold":97,"sequencer.component-multiply":98